==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kalisa, type χ''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Kalisa χ''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Ultimate Kalisa χ''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], Behemoth Stones and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Kalisa is an excellent anti-Angel attacker who acts as a very aggressive frontline heavy hitter and suicide bomber. Alone, Kalisa can take down weaker Angel enemies like [[Angelic Gory]] and [[Heavenly Hippoe]] in merely one or two hits. If timed perfectly with the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] [[Cat Cannon|Cannon]], Kalisa can rush in and deal a single attack's worth of damage to any Angel within her range.

Kalisa's weakness is her short range, which leaves her vulnerable to [[Chickful A]], [[Winged Pigge]] and especially [[Angelic Sleipnir]]; either one constantly outrange and knock Kalisa back, leaving her helpless to attack. Take care not to deploy Kalisa in the wrong time unless these enemies are frozen, weakened, or slowed. Elsewise, Kalisa will be unable to hit them, effectively wasting your money.

As with all fast cats, take care when using the Cat Cannon or other sources of knockback since it can cause her to clip through enemies and get hurt.

==='''True Form'''===
Divine Kalisa χ gains a higher attack range and more attack power. The extra range is quite nice and does not hurt, but does not improve enough to change much about her usage with the one exception being how she can now outrange Winged Pigge. This makes her a risky, but rewarding way to deal with Winged Pigge. The bigger and more important change is to her attack power, which further increases her devastation against Angels.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
At first, Ultimate Kalisa χ's improvements are unassuming. The 20% chance to create [[Explosion]]s allows her to pierce up to 680 range, nuking everything in sight for 160,000 damage per attack cycle at Lv.60 (640,000 vs. Angels). This is a very sizable increase, but only activates once every 25 seconds on average, which means clutch Explosions can't be relied on to save you at a moment's notice. You should always work with the assumption that you're playing [[Wikipedia:Murphy's Law|Murphy's Law]] Battle Cats. If an Explosion activates, great! Just don't build your game plan around it.

Where things really pick up is with the major upgrade to Kalisa's survivability. Turns out, if you give a rusher/nuker with ~19.1k generalist DPS (or ~22.9k with Attack Buff [[Talents]]) the range of a backliner, pierce through Explosions, and higher HP than she has burst damage, then what you're left with is an unstoppable force of nature. The increase from 355 —> 405 range is much more impactful than what it initially seems, as that range threshold flips an unbelievable amount of interactions to her favor, allowing her potential as a generalist attacker to finally shine through. It not only matches her up much better into Angels like Chickful A, Angelic Sleipnir, and Winged Pigge, but also keeps her completely out of reach from untargeted supports. In a way, she can be described as a backline rendition of Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], extremely high praise that should not be given out flippantly. Kalisa's individual performance is further complemented by her blazing fast 64-second recharge rate; this is almost as fast as [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]'s 51-second recharge rate, otherwise known as one of the fastest recharges for an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] rusher. All of this is to say that if one Kalisa bites the dust, another can replace her at the snap of a finger. If she doesn't die, then you'll eventually have two on the field, then three, and so on until the stage in question is utterly overrun by a girl who peaked in high school.

[[Wave Immunity]] makes her a reliable counter to [[Youcan]] and [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]], while further improving her generalist performance against a plethora of Wave Attackers, as well as the [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]]. Truthfully, [[Weaken Immunity]] doesn't do much outside of being a failsafe for [[Winged Pigge]] and the occasional [[Great Angel Chibinel]]. Regardless, it still has application against [[Calamary]] and [[Cli-One]], so the extra reliability in potentially tricky situations is never a bad thing. In short, Ultimate Kalisa χ is a very worthwhile Ultra Form.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Slow]]''' is a minor expansion to her niche, but given her role as a nuker, she already obliterates most enemies in a few clean hits, rendering their crowd-control status somewhat moot. It does help with tankier Angels, such as [[St. Dober]], [[Boraphim]], and Winged Pigge, the likes which can singlehandedly push past your defences in seconds. However, it is inconsistent at the best of times and should not be entirely depended on. Additionally, other crowd-controllers like [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]] can keep these enemies permanently Slowed regardless of whether this Talent is unlocked.

'''[[Immune to Curse]]''' is good given her mediocre standing range prior to her Ultra Form. She's likely to take many stray hits from a variety of untargeted enemies, so Kalisa getting to keep her Massive Damage and (potentially) Slow is  situationally helpful. There is also a surprisingly large number of mixed stages featuring both Relic and Angel.

'''Move Speed Up''' makes Kalisa more reckless prior to her Ultra Form, as speed clipping becomes a real concern for a select group of enemies. It does help her infiltrate enemy blind spots like [[Cruel Angel Clionel]]'s, while also sneaking in hits in between enemy attack cycles a little easier. However, her speed is simply not an issue in the slightest, and she can do both of these well enough without it, so this Talent is a bit unnecessary even if it doesn't hurt her outright.

'''Attack Buff''' is always good on a nuker, but you already know that, so there's no need to articulate why. '''HP Buff''' is fairly decent in the context of her Ultra Form specifically, since her survivability is a major focus there, where this Talent gives her an even easier time shrugging off damage.

